{"action":"opened","issue":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21649","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21649/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21649/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21649/events","html_url":"https://github.com/scipy/scipy/issues/21649","id":2559581513,"node_id":"I_kwDOABZIoc6YkB1J","number":21649,"title":"RFC: Splitting off special function scalar kernels into separate library","user":{"login":"steppi","id":1953382,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NTMzODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1953382?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/steppi","html_url":"https://github.com/steppi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/steppi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/steppi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/steppi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/steppi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/steppi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/steppi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/steppi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/steppi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/steppi/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":5432239077,"node_id":"LA_kwDOABZIoc8AAAABQ8lj5Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/labels/RFC","name":"RFC","color":"FEF2C0","default":false,"description":"Request for Comments; typically used to gather feedback for a substantial change proposal"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2024-10-01T15:25:21Z","updated_at":"2024-10-01T15:25:21Z","closed_at":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"body":"Something that's been under discussion for a while now is splitting off the scalar kernels for ufuncs and gufuncs in `scipy.special` into a separate library. The plan would be for this library to still be managed under the `scipy` organization, but it would contain GPU capable implementations of scalar kernels which could be used in other array libraries, and would be a shared dependency of at least SciPy and CuPy.

As a start, I've created the [scipy/xsf](https://github.com/scipy/xsf) repo for this purpose with the blessing of @rgommers. I wrote up a longish RFC at https://github.com/scipy/xsf/issues/1. This gives some motivation, describes the migration steps I anticipate, and gives a rough roadmap for the rest of the year. If we can get consensus for this, I'd like to complete the migration over the next month.

My intention is for this issue in SciPy as a place to discuss whether it's a good idea to split out the scalar kernels in general, and what this may mean for SciPy, while https://github.com/scipy/xsf/issues/1 is for discussing specifics of the migration plan and roadmap. I don't mean for this to be strict though; feel free to comment on either.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21649/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21649/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}}
